Id":"401869844344","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6051,"playId":"401869844348","tiePercentage":0},{"homeWinPercentage":0.6193,"playId":"401869844352","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3654","guid":"4e1c78e5-46c1-3303-8509-521b77f6b1f7","fullName":"Brooks Stadium (SC)","address":{"city":"Conway","state":"SC","zipCode":"29526","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[]},"attendance":19485},"article":{"headline":"Jaquari Lewis' 4 TD runs lead Appalachian State to 35-32 victory over Coastal Carolina","description":"— Jaquari Lewis had four touchdown runs and Appalachian State rallied to beat Coastal Carolina 35-32 on Friday night.","story":"CONWAY, S.C. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5156152/jaquari-lewis\" target=\"_new\">Jaquari Lewis</a> had four touchdown runs and Appalachian State rallied to beat Coastal Carolina 35-32 on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              Lewis carried 13 times for 85 yards for Appalachian State (4-2, 1-1 Sun Belt Conference), scoring on runs of 12, 1, 12 and 3 yards.\n\n\r\n              Mountaineers' junior backup <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5146664/henry-hasselbeck\" target=\"_new\">Henry Hasselbeck</a> completed 9 of 12 passes for 112 yards and his first touchdown — a 31-yarder to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5300543/sam-pickett\" target=\"_new\">Sam Pickett III</a> for a 35-24 lead with 6:41 remaining. He also rushed 21 times for 125 yards. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870999/malachi-singleton\" target=\"_new\">Malachi Singleton</a> started and threw for 151 yards on 12-for-14 passing.\n\n\r\n              Coastal Carolina (2-5, 1-2) grabbed a 7-0 lead on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5296439/deuce-bailey\" target=\"_new\">Deuce Bailey</a>'s 21-yard touchdown pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5296438/tristian-gardner\" target=\"_new\">Tristian Gardner</a> to start the game.\n\n\r\n              Appalachian State answered with Lewis' 12-yard touchdown run to tie it 7-7.\n\n\r\n              Singleton drove the Mountaineers 88 yards in eight plays on their second possession, scoring on Lewis' 1-yard plunge for a 14-7 lead after one quarter. \n\n\r\n              The Chanticleers pulled even early in the second quarter on Bailey's 71-yard scoring strike to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4871022/robby-washington\" target=\"_new\">Robby Washington</a>.\n\n\r\n              Bailey had an 8-yard touchdown toss to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5379841/ben-verges\" target=\"_new\">Ben Verges</a> at the end of a 13-play, 78-yard drive with 1:53 left before halftime for a 21-14 lead.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4836468/reggie-jean\" target=\"_new\">Reggie Jean</a> recovered a fumble by Singleton with 12 seconds left and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5304544/nico-cavanillas-alti\" target=\"_new\">Nico Cavanillas Alti</a> kicked a career-long 58-yard field goal to put the Chanticleers up 24-14 at halftime. Bailey connected with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5153389/colton-hinton\" target=\"_new\">Colton Hinton</a> for a 24-yard gain to set up the kick.\n\n\r\n              Lewis had another 12-yard touchdown run and App State cut it to 24-21 midway through the third quarter.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5147728/devin-henderson\" target=\"_new\">Devin Henderson</a> picked off a Bailey pass and Lewis scored on a 3-yard run 10 plays later for a 28-24 advantage heading to the final quarter.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4876695/jaden-allen\" target=\"_new\">Jaden Allen</a>-Hendrix had a 2-yard touchdown run and Coastal Carolina added the two-point conversion with 3:11 left, but the Mountaineers ran out the clock.\n\n\r\n              Bailey finished with 298 yards on 16-for-31 passing with three touchdowns and an interception. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5203477/dominic-lee-knicely\" target=\"_new\">Dominic Lee-Knicely</a> gained 90 yards on 18 rushes.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Appalachian State: Hosts James Madison on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              Coastal Carolina: At Georgia State on Oct. 31.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-10-17T03:50:26Z"}}